     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, so I'm treating them as claims. They don't change the labeled maximum, and 5,100 mg/day is double the 2,550 mg/day limit for immediate-release metformin. Metformin at that dose carries a real risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the label,** such as 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). I can also enter 850 mg twice daily if the intended total was 1,700 mg/day.\n- **Route the order through your pharmacy or the prescriber of record.** If a high-dose protocol exists, the pharmacy or an attending can enter it through a channel that has a formal override and verification step.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
